# generation: 1
# One line per container. ketsync decides placement; tp moves the data.
#
#   ct     the container id on its home node
#   tier   which copy pool it belongs in: ssd (comes back fast) or hdd
#   home   the node it normally runs on, by NAME (looked up in nodes.tsv)
#   dr     the node that picks it up when home is gone, by NAME
#
# dr is written down rather than chosen at the time. Placing a customer by
# free RAM at 3am is how a customer ends up on the wrong machine; the same
# rule as tp's "no defaults, never guess". Override once with --node if the
# day comes and the written answer is wrong.
#
# ct   tier  home            dr
110	hdd	pve-r32	pve-r33
120	hdd	pve-r33	pve-r32
